{
 "format": "mainaiger",
 "schema_version": 2,
 "notebook": {
  "nbformat": 4,
  "nbformat_minor": 5,
  "metadata": {
   "kernelspec": {
    "name": "python3",
    "display_name": "Python 3",
    "language": "python"
   },
   "mainaiger": {
    "example": true,
    "name": "self-improve-repo",
    "title": "Self-improvement loop on a repository (copy, change, test, judge, loop)"
   }
  },
  "cells": [
   {
    "id": "readme",
    "cell_type": "markdown",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "How this loop works"
     }
    },
    "source": "# Self-improvement loop on a repository\n\nThe session's workspace must be a checkout of a repository (for MainAIger itself: this repository). **Copy repository** copies it into the session's own `/tmp` (the workspace stays read-only), **Baseline tests** runs the test module you name there, **Read the file** prints the file you name, **Propose change** asks a model for ONE find/replace change for the task you typed, **Apply to copy** restores the file from the workspace and applies the change to the copy (never the checkout), **Run tests** runs the same tests in the copy, **Judge** decides keep / revert / ask from the diff and the test output, and the dashed loop arrow sends the run back to **Propose** (at most twice) while the verdict is not \"keep\", with the previous attempt pasted into the next prompt. **Report** prints every attempt and, for a keep, the patch to apply with `git apply` in your checkout.\n\nFill the form on **Task**: what to change, which file, which test module (dotted, e.g. `tests.test_decide`). Needs a running session, a workspace, and an installed Ollama model named in the two model cells (Models page). Keep the test module small: a cell has 60 seconds.\n",
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "task",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Task",
      "form": {
       "fields": [
        {
         "name": "task",
         "type": "text",
         "label": "What to change (one small step)",
         "default": "Add a one-line comment above extract_json explaining what it does"
        },
        {
         "name": "file",
         "type": "text",
         "label": "File to change (relative to the repository)",
         "default": "local_lab/decide.py"
        },
        {
         "name": "test_module",
         "type": "text",
         "label": "Test module to run (dotted)",
         "default": "tests.test_decide"
        },
        {
         "name": "max_lines",
         "type": "integer",
         "label": "Lines of the file shown to the model",
         "default": 400
        }
       ],
       "values": {}
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"task:\", task)\nprint(\"file:\", file, \"| tests:\", test_module)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "copy",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Copy repository"
     }
    },
    "source": "# Copy the repository into the session's own temporary folder; the workspace stays read-only.\nimport os, shutil, sys\nSRC = \"/workspace\" if os.path.isdir(\"/workspace\") else os.getcwd()\nDST = \"/tmp/mainaiger-repo\"\nSKIP = {\".git\", \"node_modules\", \"__pycache__\", \"dist\", \".venv\", \"venv\", \".pytest_cache\", \"build\"}\nshutil.rmtree(DST, ignore_errors=True)\ncopied = 0\nfor root, dirs, files in os.walk(SRC):\n    dirs[:] = [d for d in dirs if d not in SKIP]\n    rel = os.path.relpath(root, SRC)\n    os.makedirs(os.path.join(DST, rel) if rel != \".\" else DST, exist_ok=True)\n    for name in files:\n        try:\n            shutil.copy2(os.path.join(root, name), os.path.join(DST, rel, name) if rel != \".\" else os.path.join(DST, name))\n            copied += 1\n        except OSError:\n            pass\nprint(\"copied %d files from %s to %s\" % (copied, SRC, DST))\nif not os.path.isfile(os.path.join(DST, file)):\n    raise SystemExit(\"the file %r is not in the repository\" % file)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "baseline",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Baseline tests"
     }
    },
    "source": "# The named tests, in the untouched copy: the bar every proposal must clear.\nimport subprocess, sys\ndef run_tests():\n    r = subprocess.run([sys.executable, \"-m\", \"unittest\", test_module], cwd=DST, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=50)\n    tail = \"\\n\".join((r.stdout + r.stderr).strip().splitlines()[-12:])\n    return r.returncode == 0, tail\nbaseline_ok, baseline_text = run_tests()\nprint(\"baseline:\", \"OK\" if baseline_ok else \"FAILED\")\nprint(baseline_text)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "read",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Read the file"
     }
    },
    "source": "# What the model sees: the file, with line numbers, up to max_lines lines.\nimport os\nwith open(os.path.join(DST, file), encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as handle:\n    file_lines = handle.read().splitlines()\nprint(\"file:\", file, \"(%d lines%s)\" % (len(file_lines), \"\" if len(file_lines) <= max_lines else \", first %d shown\" % max_lines))\nfor number, text in enumerate(file_lines[:max_lines], 1):\n    print(\"%4d  %s\" % (number, text))\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "propose",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Propose change",
      "model": {
       "model": "qwen2.5-coder:7b",
       "output": "proposal",
       "attempts": 2,
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
         "find": {
          "type": "string"
         },
         "replace": {
          "type": "string"
         },
         "why": {
          "type": "string",
          "maxLength": 300
         }
        },
        "required": [
         "find",
         "replace",
         "why"
        ]
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "You change code in a repository, one small step at a time. Standard library Python only unless the file already imports more.\n\n{{output:Task}}\n\nThe previous attempt, if there was one (do not repeat it):\n{{output:Apply to copy}}\n{{output:Run tests}}\n\nThe file (line numbers are not part of the file):\n{{output:Read the file}}\n\nPropose ONE change as a find/replace. \"find\" must be copied verbatim from the file (at least one complete line, without the line numbers) and occur exactly once; \"replace\" is the new text for those lines; \"why\" is one sentence. Keep the file valid Python.\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "apply",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Apply to copy"
     }
    },
    "source": "# Restore the file from the workspace, then apply the proposal to the COPY only; show the diff.\nimport difflib, os, shutil\noriginal_path = os.path.join(SRC, file); copy_path = os.path.join(DST, file)\nshutil.copy2(original_path, copy_path)\nwith open(copy_path, encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\") as handle:\n    before = handle.read()\ntry:\n    history\nexcept NameError:\n    history = []\nattempt = {\"why\": proposal.get(\"why\", \"\"), \"applied\": False, \"diff\": \"\", \"error\": None}\ncount = before.count(proposal[\"find\"]) if proposal.get(\"find\") else 0\nif count != 1:\n    attempt[\"error\"] = \"the 'find' text occurs %d times in %s (it must occur exactly once)\" % (count, file)\nelse:\n    after = before.replace(proposal[\"find\"], proposal[\"replace\"], 1)\n    try:\n        compile(after, file, \"exec\")\n    except SyntaxError as error:\n        attempt[\"error\"] = \"the result is not valid Python: line %s: %s\" % (error.lineno, error.msg)\n    else:\n        with open(copy_path, \"w\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as handle:\n            handle.write(after)\n        attempt[\"applied\"] = True\n        attempt[\"diff\"] = \"\".join(difflib.unified_diff(before.splitlines(True), after.splitlines(True), \"a/\" + file, \"b/\" + file))\nhistory.append(attempt)\nprint(\"attempt %d\" % len(history))\nprint(\"why:\", attempt[\"why\"])\nif attempt[\"applied\"]:\n    print(attempt[\"diff\"])\nelse:\n    print(\"the proposal could not be applied:\", attempt[\"error\"])\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "tests",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Run tests"
     }
    },
    "source": "# The same tests, in the changed copy.\nif history[-1][\"applied\"]:\n    tests_ok, tests_text = run_tests()\nelse:\n    tests_ok, tests_text = False, \"(not run: the proposal could not be applied)\"\nhistory[-1][\"tests_ok\"] = tests_ok\nprint(\"tests after the change:\", \"OK\" if tests_ok else \"FAILED\")\nprint(tests_text)\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "judge",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Judge",
      "model": {
       "model": "qwen2.5-coder:7b",
       "output": "verdict",
       "schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
         "action": {
          "type": "string",
          "enum": [
           "keep",
           "revert",
           "ask"
          ]
         },
         "confidence": {
          "type": "number"
         },
         "reasons": {
          "type": "array",
          "items": {
           "type": "string"
          },
          "maxItems": 3
         }
        },
        "required": [
         "action",
         "confidence"
        ]
       }
      }
     }
    },
    "source": "A change was applied to a copy of a repository and its tests were run.\n{{output:Task}}\n\nThe change:\n{{output:Apply to copy}}\n\nThe tests afterwards:\n{{output:Run tests}}\n\nDecide: \"keep\" only if the change was applied, the tests pass, and it does what the task asked; \"revert\" if the tests fail, the change could not be applied, or it does something else; \"ask\" if you cannot tell. Give up to three short reasons.\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   },
   {
    "id": "report",
    "cell_type": "code",
    "metadata": {
     "mainaiger": {
      "title": "Report"
     }
    },
    "source": "print(\"=\" * 56)\nprint(\"Repository self-improvement loop: %d attempt%s\" % (len(history), \"\" if len(history) == 1 else \"s\"))\nprint(\"=\" * 56)\nprint(\"task:\", task)\nprint(\"file:\", file, \"| tests:\", test_module, \"| baseline:\", \"OK\" if baseline_ok else \"FAILED\")\nfor i, h in enumerate(history, 1):\n    state = (\"tests OK\" if h.get(\"tests_ok\") else \"tests FAILED\") if h[\"applied\"] else \"not applied: \" + str(h[\"error\"])\n    print(\"  %d. %s - %s\" % (i, state, h[\"why\"]))\nprint(\"last verdict:\", verdict[\"action\"], \"(confidence %.2f)\" % verdict[\"confidence\"])\nfor r in verdict.get(\"reasons\", []):\n    print(\" -\", r)\nif verdict[\"action\"] == \"keep\" and history[-1][\"applied\"]:\n    print()\n    print(\"Nothing was written to your checkout. To keep this change, save the patch below as change.patch\")\n    print(\"in your checkout and run: git apply change.patch   (then read it, run the full suite, commit)\")\n    print(\"-\" * 56)\n    print(history[-1][\"diff\"])\nelif verdict[\"action\"] == \"ask\":\n    print(\"Could not tell after the loop's budget: run again, narrow the task, or name a more specific test module.\")\nelse:\n    print(\"Every attempt was reverted: the checkout is untouched. Run again for new proposals, or narrow the task.\")\n",
    "execution_count": null,
    "outputs": []
   }
  ]
 },
